enchilada: UFS: read-only reader for one partition on another LUN (modem firmware, mss=2+)

The modem firmware is read where the phone keeps it: modem_a, /dev/block/sde4, i.e. UFS LUN 4
(sha256 of the partition = backup/modem-fw/modem_a.img). sweet_ufs_read_part(lun, name, off,
dst, len) finds the partition in that LUN's GPT (ufs_find_partition, which now returns the bounds
instead of setting the root partition's), clears a unit attention with up to three TEST UNIT
READYs as init does, and copies the byte range out through the 1 MiB bounce buffer with
READ(10) only; ranges outside the partition are refused. su.lun is switched only while
sweet_ufs_lock is held and is restored before it is dropped, and every write (strategy, the
sweetlog thread) takes the same lock, so a write can never be issued to another LUN; the root
partition's bounds (the write fence) are not touched. Same approach as ios-topaz 0115.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
